From 9a1aca7bc09af752951b4803743966cc3f559ad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmirSalahY <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 12:30:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/27] fix(ui): don't pick nerd icons for a terminal that
 can't render them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A font being installed doesn't mean the terminal uses it. With MesloLGS NF
installed and selected in iTerm, the VS Code/Cursor integrated terminal had no
font configured, fell back to Menlo, and drew every icon as tofu.

Detection now also reads terminal.integrated.fontFamily (falling back to
editor.fontFamily) from the settings.json of whichever VS Code fork is running,
identified by trying the known app dirs since they all report TERM_PROGRAM=vscode.
Other terminals are assumed configured rather than guessed at — silently dropping
to the plain set on a working terminal gives the user no signal.

is doctor now distinguishes 'no font installed' from 'font installed but this
terminal isn't using it' and names the setting to change.

Logic is exposed as pure helpers (isNerdFontName, parseVscodeFontSetting,
scanForNerdFont) because jest's process.env is a JS-side copy that native
os.homedir() ignores, so $HOME-based fixtures silently test the real machine.
